{"schema":"zzx-html-edition-profile-v1","country":"TO","name":"Tonga","year":2007,"status":"source-extracted; field review pending","source":{"name":"factbook-2007.zip","member":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html","sha256":"c18546da4fd63a5a090397b470f3dbc6445a3aac260332d15b83d3774870d0a6","format":"html"},"rights_notice_member":"factbook-2007/docs/contributor_copyright.html","rights_notice_sha256":"0aa0c111c3015a738f223e5be4ed3275a829514a52d1781742a8671e915bdb1e","fields":[{"category":"introduction","label":"Background","content":"Tonga - unique among Pacific nations - never completely lost its indigenous governance. The archipelagos of \"The Friendly Islands\" were united into a Polynesian kingdom in 1845. Tonga became a constitutional monarchy in 1875 and a British protectorate in 1900; it withdrew from the protectorate and joined the Commonwealth of Nations in 1970. Tonga remains the only monarchy in the Pacific.","ordinal":1,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:1","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"geography","label":"Location","content":"Oceania, archipelago in the South Pacific Ocean, about two-thirds of the way from Hawaii to New Zealand","ordinal":2,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:2","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"geography","label":"Geographic coordinates","content":"20 00 S, 175 00 W","ordinal":3,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:3","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"geography","label":"Map references","content":"Oceania","ordinal":4,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:4","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"geography","label":"Area","content":"total: 748 sq km\n\nland: 718 sq km\n\nwater: 30 sq km","ordinal":5,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:5","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"geography","label":"Area - comparative","content":"four times the size of Washington, DC","ordinal":6,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:6","country":"TO","ed