ry":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Capital","content":"name: Nuku'alofa\n\ngeographic coordinates: 21 08 S, 175 12 W\n\ntime difference: UTC+13 (18 hours ahead of Washington, DC during Standard Time)","ordinal":41,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:41","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Administrative divisions","content":"3 island groups; Ha'apai, Tongatapu, Vava'u","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:42","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"4 June 1970 (from UK protectorate)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:43","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Emancipation Day, 4 June (1970)","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:44","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"4 November 1875; revised 1 January 1967","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:45","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"based on English common law","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:46","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"21 years of age; universal","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:47","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: King George TUPOU V (since 11 September 2006)\n\nhead of government: Prime Minister Dr. Feleti SEVELE (since 11 February 2006); Deputy Prime Minister Dr. Viliami TANGI (since 16 May 2006)\n\ncabinet: Cabinet consists of 14 members, 10 appointed by the monarch for life; four appointed from among the elected members of the Legislative Assembly, including two each from the nobles' and peoples' representatives serving three-year terms\n\nnote: there is also a Privy Council that consists of the monarch, the cabinet, and two governors\n\nelections: none; the monarch is hereditary; prime minister and deputy prime minister appointed by the monarch","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:48","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral Legislative Assembly or Fale Alea (32 seats - 14 reserved for cabinet ministers sitting ex officio, nine for nobles selected by the country's 33 nobles, and nine elected by popular vote; members serve three-year terms)\n\nelections: last held on 21 March 2005 (next to be held in 2008)\n\nelection results: Peoples Representatives: percent of vote - HRDMT 70%, other 30%; seats - HRDMT 7, independents 2","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:49","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Supreme Court (judges are appointed by the monarch); Court of Appeal (Chief Justice and high court justices from overseas chosen and approved by Privy Council)","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:50","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"People's Democratic Party [Tesina FUKO]","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:51","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"Human Rights and Democracy Movement Tonga or HRDMT [Rev. Simote VEA, chairman]; Public Servant's Association [Finau TUTONE]","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:52","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"ACP, AsDB, C, FAO, G-77, IBRD, ICAO, ICRM, IDA, IFAD, IFC, IFRCS, IHO, IMF, IMO, Interpol, IOC, ITU, ITUC, OPCW, PIF, Sparteca, SPC, UN, UNCTAD, UNESCO, UNIDO, UPU, WCO, WHO, WIPO, WMO, WTO (observer)","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:53","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"chief of mission: Ambassador Fekitamoeloa 'UTOIKAMANU\n\nchancery: 250 East 51st Street, New York, NY 10022\n\ntelephone: [1] (917) 369-1025\n\nFAX: [1] (917) 369-1024\n\nconsulate(s) general: San Francisco","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:54","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"the US does not have an embassy in Tonga; the ambassador to Fiji is accredited to Tonga","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:55","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"red with a bold red cross on a white rectangle in the upper hoist-side corner","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:56","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Tonga has a small, open, South Pacific island economy. It has a narrow export base in agricultural goods. Squash, coconuts, bananas, and vanilla beans are the main crops, and agricultural exports make up two-thirds of total exports. The country must import a high proportion of its food, mainly from New Zealand. The country remains dependent on external aid and remittances from Tongan communities overseas to offset its trade deficit. Tourism is the second-largest source of hard currency earnings following remittances. The government is emphasizing the development of the private sector, especially the encouragement of investment, and is committing increased funds for health and education. Tonga has a reasonably sound basic infrastructure and well-developed social services. High unemployment among the young, a continuing upturn in inflation, pressures for democratic reform, and rising civil service expenditures are major issues facing the government.","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:57","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$178.5 million (2004 est.)","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:58","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (official exchange rate)","content":"$244 million (2005 est.)","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:59","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"2.4% (2005 est.)","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:60","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita (PPP)","content":"$2,200 (2005 est.)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:61","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: 23%\n\nindustry: 27%\n\nservices: 50% (FY03/04 est.)","ordinal":62,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:62","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"33,910 (2003)","ordinal":63,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:63","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force - by occupation","content":"agriculture: 65%\n\nindustry and services: 35% (1997 est.)","ordinal":64,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:64","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Unemployment rate","content":"13% (FY03/04 est.)","ordinal":65,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:65","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Population below poverty line","content":"24% (FY03/04)","ordinal":66,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tn.html#field:66","country":"TO","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Household income or consumption by percentage share","content":"lowest 10%: NA%\n\nhi